\pard\widctlpar\sa100\sl300\slmult1\ql\fs24 The within-university results show both appearances and disappearances of category terminology (Table 3). Research-data and database terminology changes from absent to present in 57 pairs and from present to absent in 24. Software terminology appears in 48 pairs and disappears in 27. Invention or patent terminology is already present at both endpoints of most comparisons. These results indicate that the recorded vocabulary is not static. They do not establish that newly named objects were previously outside an institutional claim. An earlier umbrella definition may already have covered them; a later mention may instead identify an exception.\par

